 "notes": [
  "Every line of the committed summary texts and gae-band outputs was re-derived from the CSVs by the validator's own code and compared byte for byte: H1-hsweep-run-20261018T2240Z/hsweep_summary.txt: 77 lines, identical True; H2-glue-run-20261018T2240Z/glue_summary.txt: 34 lines, identical True; H4-memsweep-run-20261018T2209Z/memsweep_summary.txt: 7 lines, identical True; H6-large-run-20261018T2210Z/summary.txt: 10 lines, identical True; H6-large-run-20261018T2210Z/routes_summary.csv: 37 lines, identical True; H6-large-run-20261018T2210Z/ranking.csv: 5 lines, identical True; gae-band/H2-glue-run-20261018T2240Z.txt: 32 lines, identical True; gae-band/H6-large-run-20261018T2210Z.txt: 16 lines, identical True. No line of the CSVs contradicts a summary.",
  "Symmetry: arm R is rho on E(F_{p^2}) with the negation map (r = 64 adding walk, distinguished points, Bos-Kleinjung-Lenstra fruitless-cycle handling). The verifier computed j(E) for every replayed instance: j is never in F_p and never 0 or 1728 (char p >= 1091). So Aut(E) over the algebraic closure is {+-1}: no small-order automorphism beyond negation exists; and since j^p != j, E is not isomorphic to its conjugate E^sigma, so no GLS-style twisted Frobenius of order 2 or 4 acts on E(F_{p^2}). A map psi = phi o Frobenius built from an isogeny phi: E^sigma -> E has degree p*deg(phi) > 1, so it is not an automorphism and does not give rho equivalence classes (reasoned, not measured). Negation is therefore the strongest symmetry available to rho on these curves. Same binary and unit: arms R and IC run in the same n2_routes process and thread, on the same instance, base point and target, with the same thread-local counters (F_p mult M; F_{p^2} mul 3M, sqr 2M, inv 1I + 4M; hashing / table lookups / LA mod ell as native ops), and are priced by the same cost function. Coverage of this check: 158 distinct curves in this study's replay dumps, against 158 distinct recorded instances (distinct (p, ell) in the CSVs).",
  "H1: alpha_J = 0.4022 with the bootstrap replicated exactly (xorshift seed 0xa1fa, 2000 resamples): [0.3801, 0.4239], entirely below 1/2 as frozen in the decision rule. Rho's own fit is alpha_R = 0.4680 [0.4455, 0.4897], which excludes the theoretical 1/2: in H1 the rho arm runs on average ~8% above 0.886/sqrt(h) at large h (cell ratios up to 1.25; z ~ 4 in two cells, s.e. from 4 instances). That makes the reference slightly weaker than ideal at large h (it favours the IC) and does not change the H1 verdict.",
  "H2 gate three points (I = 3M, measured Jacobian op 41.3M + 1.00I, Legendre split test at one I per Jglue step (H3), native 0 / 0.1 / 1 GAE): rho is cheaper at all three points at 40 bits, h = 1 (IC/rho 1.78 / 1.80 / 1.88). Distance to the matched rho at measured cost: about 1.8x. The full Erratum V band (12 cells, incl. the IC-favourable price) is unresolved at h = 1 (0.759-1.876) and rho-cheaper at h = 4 for 36/40 bits.",
  "Report-text inconsistency (IC-favourable, small): REPORT_ROUND4.md (pinned tree) gives the h = 1 distance to rho as 'about 1.7x at 40 bits under measured costs', which is glue_summary.txt's 'Jglue/rho cost ratio (measured, I=3M, w=0) 1.677'. That line prices walk_M + 3*walk_I only and omits the H3 Legendre split test (one I per Jglue step) that Addendum H3 and the band use; with it the same point is 1.7775 (the gate point at w = 0, and the 1.78x in the later erratum text). All glue_summary lines reproduce exactly; only the report's choice of line understates the gap by ~6%.",
  "H2 rho reference at h = 1: steps/p 0.956 / 0.844 / 0.778 / 0.860 at 28 / 32 / 36 / 40 bits vs 0.886 theory (all within ~1.1 s.e.); not weak at the gate row (40 bits).",
